{
  "title": "Ziyarate Imam Musa Kazim (a.s.)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكَ یَا نُوْرَا اللّٰهِ فِیْ ظُلُمَاتِ الْاَرْضِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya nuran allahi fi zulumati al-ardi\nPeace be upon you, O light of Allah in the darkness of the earth,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَلِیَّ اللّٰهِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya waliyya allahi\npeace be upon you, O intimate friend of Allah,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكَ یَا حُجَّۃَ اللّٰهِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya hujjata allahi\npeace be upon you, O Argument of Allah,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكَ یَا بَابَ اللّٰهِ\nalssalamu `alayka ya baba allahi\npeace be upon you, O gate of Allah.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلوٰۃَ\nashhadu annaka aqamta alssalata\nI bear witness that you established the prayer,\nوَ اٰتَیْتَ الزَّكوٰۃَ\nwa atayta alzzakata\nand paid the poor-rate,\nوَ اَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ\nwa amarta bilma`rufi\nand enjoined what is right,\nوَ نَهَیْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ\nwa nahayta `ani almunkari\nand forbade what is wrong,\nوَ تَلَوْتَ الْكِتَابَ حَقَّ تِلاَوَتِهٖ\nwa talawta alkitaba haqqa tilawatihi\nand recited the Book as it should truly be recited,\nوَ جَاهَدْتَ فِیْ اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ\nwa jahadta fi allahi haqqa jihadihi\nand strove for the sake of Allah as one should truly strive,\nوَ صَبَرْتَ عَلَی الْأذَیٰ فِیْ جَنْبِهٖ مُحْتَسِباً\nwa sabarta `ala al-adha fi janbihi muhtasiban\nand patiently bore harm for His sake, seeking reward,\nوَ عَبَدْتَهٗ مُخْلِصاً\nwa `abadtahu mukhlisan\nand worshipped Him sincerely,\nحَتیّٰ اَتَاكَ الْیَقِیْنُ\nhatta ataka alyaqinu\nuntil certainty (death) came to you.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ اَوْلیٰ بِاللّٰهِ وَ بِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَ\nashhadu annaka awla billahi wa birasulihi\nI bear witness that you are most worthy in relation to Allah and His Messenger,\nاَنَّكَ ابْنُ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ حَقًّا\nwa annaka ibnu rasuli allahi haqqan\nand that you are truly the son of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَبْرَئُ اِلَی اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَعْدَائِكَ\nabra'u ila allahi min a`da'ika\nI disavow before Allah your enemies,\nوَ اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَی اللّٰهِ بِمَوَالاَتِكَ\nwa ataqarrabu ila allahi bimuwalatika\nand I seek nearness to Allah through my loyalty to you.\nاَتَیْتُكَ یَا مُوَلاَیَ عَارِفاً بِحَقِّكَ\nataytuka ya mawlaya `arifan bihaqqika\nI have come to you, O my master, knowing your right,\nمُوَالِیاً لِاَوْلِیَائِكَ مَعَادِیاً لِاَعْدَائِكَ\nmuwaliyan li'awliya'ika mu`adiyan li'a`da'ika\nloyal to your friends, hostile to your enemies,\nفَاشْفَعْ لِیْ عَنْدَ رَبِّكَ۔\nfashfa` li `inda rabbika\nso intercede for me with your Lord."
}
